cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this project's audit procedure or results, please cite this
  repository and the dataset (see data/LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md).
type: software
title: 'Brain Tumor MRI Classification — and an audit of the benchmark everyone gets 99% on'
authors:
  - family-names: Arya
    given-names: Rishab
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Rishabharya810/brain-tumor-mri-classification'
abstract: >-
  Four-class brain-tumor MRI classification with a data-quality audit:
  73% of the benchmark's test set shares a perceptual hash with its training
  split. Dual metrics (96.31% full test / 89.50% on the 438 leak-free images),
  a 90k-parameter baseline, 3-seed stability, and Grad-CAM failure analysis.
keywords:
  - brain-tumor
  - mri
  - classification
  - data-leakage
  - benchmark-audit
  - pytorch
license: MIT
